        "interpretation": "The pinned R595 UVM creates its CE proxy pool only when the parent GPU is SR-IOV Heavy. Paging-channel allocate, destroy, and push are used only for those proxy channels. PagingChannelsMap/Unmap are separate: the pinned uvm_rm_mem.c calls them only for proxy-VA mappings, with Map returning before the callback unless the same SR-IOV-heavy predicate is true, and Unmap requiring a previously recorded proxy mapping. The hybrid bridge's fail-closed paging callbacks therefore do not block the ordinary non-SR-IOV-heavy path. This is a source-level conclusion for the pinned trees. It does not establish the virtualization mode reported by the PC3 V100 guest or validate UVM on a GPU.",
